    <channel>
        <title>DuoUpdater</title>
        <!--
          The Sparkle feed. `scripts/publish-release.sh` regenerates this file on
          every release and pushes it here. The app reads it through
          https://updates.duoupdater.app/appcast.xml (workers/appcast relays this
          file); builds before that read
          https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jizhi0v0/duo-updater/main/appcast.xml
          directly, so this path must keep working.

          Deliberately empty rather than absent: an appcast with no items means
          "nothing newer available", which Sparkle handles as up-to-date, whereas
          a missing file is a fetch error on every check. The first release fills
          it in.

          Release history starts here. Earlier builds were published from a
          separate binary-only repo that existed only while the source was
          private, and are not carried over.
        -->
        <item>
            <title>0.5.20</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 01:56:10 +0800</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/jizhi0v0/duo-updater/releases/tag/v0.5.20</link>
            <sparkle:version>138</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.5.20</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[**Setapp beta updates are reported honestly.** DuoUpdater can only read Setapp's stable catalogue. If you have Setapp's beta updates switched on, an app that cannot be checked now says so — with a note pointing at Setapp — instead of being called current.

**A Setapp copy that is ahead of the stable catalogue is named, not “downgraded”.** If you tried a Setapp beta, its row used to show the older stable version after a down arrow, as if a downgrade were on offer. It now reads “(Setapp Beta)” when Setapp's own record still knows that build, and “(ahead of Setapp's stable releases)” otherwise; nothing is offered to install.

**Setapp editions show the app's release notes.** Where DuoUpdater already reads the vendor's notes, the Setapp copy of the same app now uses them too instead of an empty pane. Bartender 7 is the exception: our notes cover Bartender 6 only.
]]></description>
